---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Controlled execution for AI-directed robots" description="VolnLabs builds Actryn for controlled robot execution and continues AxiomOS research into runtime-programmable robot kernels.">
  <div class="min">
    <main id="main-content">
      <a href="/research#papers" class="pill quiet"><span class="dot"></span>2 papers accepted at NeurIPS 2026</a>

      <h1>Controlled execution for AI-directed robots<span class="accent">.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">VolnLabs builds systems for the point where an AI agent’s proposal becomes a physical action.</p>

      <h2>Products and research</h2>
      <div class="wide-stack">
        <section class="product-row">
          <div class="meta">Product · current focus</div>
          <div class="stack">
            <h3>Actryn</h3>
            <p>A bounded execution path from an AI agent to a robot controller. It keeps operation identity, authority, cancellation and recovery explicit when replies are lost or systems restart.</p>
            <p><a href="/actryn">See how Actryn works</a></p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="product-row">
          <div class="meta">Research · continuing</div>
          <div class="stack">
            <h3>AxiomOS</h3>
            <p>A standalone, runtime-programmable robot kernel exploring how robots can accept new behavior within explicit limits on authority and physical effects.</p>
            <p><a href="/axiomos">Explore AxiomOS</a></p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>

      <h2>Why this matters</h2>
      <div class="stack">
        <p><strong>Agents can propose robot actions.</strong> The robot still has to decide whether an operation is authorized, what limits apply, how long authority lasts and what happens when the outcome is uncertain.</p>
        <p><strong>Physical actions cannot be rolled back.</strong> A timeout cannot prove that a robot did or did not move. Execution and recovery have to preserve what is known instead of guessing.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Work with us</h2>
      <p>We are looking for an inspection-robot OEM or integrator to evaluate one bounded workflow on a controller they already run.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a href="/contact">Discuss a pilot</a>
        <a href="/research" class="secondary">Read the research</a>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</Base>
